## Hints for Future Agents
reporting.md line 6-8 contains an explicit instruction to load the
technical-writing skill when authoring a document. That sentence exists
because a semantic description match misses the common case where the model
decides mid-task to write a README section. Do not delete it as redundant
with the skill description; it is the mitigation for skills not firing.

The skill states precedence against humanizer explicitly (procedural text ->
this file wins; narrative prose -> humanizer wins). Two skills with opposite
voice guidance will otherwise fight over a runbook.

## Codebase Discoveries
Skill frontmatter convention in this plugin is inconsistent: humanizer has a
`version` key, most others do not; several use `context: fork`;
diataxis-documentation uses `allowed-tools` with Read/Write/Edit, which is
what this skill matches.

